QuestionText:
Consider the following HTML and CSS code snippet:
HTML:
<div class="container">
  <p id="hero-text" class="highlight">Olympiad Excellence</p>
</div>

CSS:
div p { color: red !important; }
#hero-text { color: blue; }
.highlight { color: green; }
p { color: orange; }

What will be the rendered text color of 'Olympiad Excellence' based on CSS Specificity and Cascade rules?

An administrator executes the following SQL statement on a Relational Database management system:
SELECT DeptID, COUNT(EmpID) FROM Employees WHERE Salary > 50000 GROUP BY DeptID HAVING COUNT(EmpID) > 3;
Identify the correct logical execution order of the clauses implemented by the database engine.

Consider the following CSS rules applied to a text block:
span {
  font-size: 16px;
}
div.parent {
  font-size: 2em;
}
p.child {
  font-size: 0.5rem;
}
If the root HTML document base font size is configured at 12px, what will be the rendered pixel font size of text inside an element styled as `p.child`?

A web developer writes the following CSS code block:
.box {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50px;
  left: 100px;
}
With this configuration, what element coordinates container baseline does the web browser use to map the 50px top and 100px left offsets?

An enterprise database manager executes this SQL command sequence:
ALTER TABLE Projects ADD CONSTRAINT UniqueProjectCode UNIQUE (ProjectCode);
What type of language category is this statement, and what change does it apply to the database schema?

Consider this CSS styling block assigned to a paragraph tag:
p {
  color: blue;
  font-size: 14px;
}
If this paragraph is nested inside an HTML parent container styled with `color: red; font-size: 24px; text-transform: uppercase;`, how will the paragraph text be rendered?

Consider the following CSS positioning rules applied to an element layout block:
.element-node {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  right: 0;
}
Where will the web browser place this element on the page, and how does it behave when the user scrolls down?
